/*
Time complexity - O(n) - each index is pushed one and popped once
Space complexity - O(n) - worst case - all elements are decreasing and have to be stored on stack 
INTUITION
Use a stack to store indexes of days whose next warmer day has not been found yet.
The stack will maintain temperatures in monotonically decreasing order.

Iterate through each day (i):

While the stack is not empty and the current temperature is warmer than the temperature at the top index:

This means we found the next warmer day for the top index.

Pop that index from the stack.

The number of days to wait = i - poppedIndex, store this in ans[poppedIndex].

Push the current index i onto the stack (because its warmer day is still unknown).

After the loop ends, any remaining indexes in the stack have no warmer future day, so set their answers to 0.

Return the ans array.

*/



class Solution {
    public int[] dailyTemperatures(int[] temperatures) {
        int n = temperatures.length;
        int[] ans = new int[n];
        Stack<Integer> id = new Stack();
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            while(!id.isEmpty() && temperatures[id.peek()]<temperatures[i]){
                int ansid = id.pop();
                ans[ansid]=i-ansid;
            }
            id.push(i);
            
        }
        while(!id.isEmpty()){
            int ansid = id.pop();
            ans[ansid]=0;
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
